 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Mesh-Open2-Closed Algorithm
-An algorithm to universally enclose open reconstructed mesh surfaces (specifically those with a single hole) by appending a base plane, creating a closed mesh suitable for MPM/FEM simulation [S2]. It differs from the standard MC boundary cap by not relying on the grid structure of the Marching Cubes output, but rather on the boundary edges of any reconstructed mesh [S2]. Input: Mesh vertices $\mathcal{V}$ and triangles $\mathcal{F}$ structured in 2D arrays [S2]. Steps: 1. Construct boundary edges and organize in a list [S2]. 2. Classify edges using a non-manifold test (manifold edges are in 2 triangles; non-manifold are boundary edges) [S2]. 3. Conduct BFS to sort boundary vertices into an ordered list [S2]. 4. Iteratively build a base plane of the soft tissue surface in the shape of the open mesh boundary [S2]. 5. Loop for each vertex $v$ in the ordered edge list: find the projection of $v$ in the appended base [S2]. 6. Connect the projection of the last $v$, the projection of the current $v$, and the center of the base plane to create new faces [S2]. Pitfall: Designed for input meshes with a single 'hole' (one connected edge). If there are two disjoint surfaces, run the algorithm separately for each surface [S2].
